  <data>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="10" width="400" height="20">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(39,121,167,1)" wrap="false" textAlign="left">
        <p>04 - CROSS-CUTTING</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="30" width="848" height="34">
      <content textType="title" fontSize="24" fontFamily="Inter" bold="true" color="rgba(15,36,64,1)" wrap="false" textAlign="left">
        <p>Security and observability: built in, not bolted on</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <line startX="56" startY="64" endX="904" endY="64">
      <border color="rgb(39, 121, 167)" width="2"/>
    </line>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="92" width="400" height="26">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="16" fontFamily="Inter" bold="true" color="rgba(15,36,64,1)" wrap="false" textAlign="left">
        <p>Card data - what we keep</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="136" width="420" height="210">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13.5" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(61,74,92,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.4" textAlign="left">
        <ul>
          <li><p>Only the last four digits are stored and returned.</p></li>
          <li><p>PAN and cvv: never at rest, never in responses, never in logs.</p></li>
          <li><p>toString() masking in DTOs - even a careless debug log cannot leak card data.</p></li>
          <li><p>Ids are opaque tokens - nothing sensitive sits in URLs.</p></li>
        </ul>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="380" width="420" height="88">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(138,148,166,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.35" textAlign="left">
        <p>Scope note: card data is not tokenized - in production the first change would be a tokenization service in front of storage.</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <line startX="484" startY="92" endX="484" endY="470">
      <border color="rgb(214, 222, 232)" width="1"/>
    </line>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="520" topLeftY="92" width="384" height="26">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="16" fontFamily="Inter" bold="true" color="rgba(15,36,64,1)" wrap="false" textAlign="left">
        <p>Observability - what is exposed</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="520" topLeftY="136" width="384" height="210">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13.5" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(61,74,92,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.4" textAlign="left">
        <ul>
          <li><p>Health probe: /actuator/health</p></li>
          <li><p>Metrics: /actuator/prometheus - payments.processed, payments.replayed, failure counters.</p></li>
          <li><p>Audit log: structured, with id and status - no card data.</p></li>
          <li><p>The audit guard keeps every number honest - INIT is never counted as processed.</p></li>
        </ul>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="520" topLeftY="380" width="384" height="88">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(138,148,166,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.35" textAlign="left">
        <p>Failures throw before the audit node - so the metrics only ever reflect terminal, truthful states.</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="856" topLeftY="510" width="48" height="18">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(138,148,166,1)" textAlign="right" wrap="false">
        <p>19 / 24</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
  </data>
  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>Two cross-cutting concerns. On security: we keep only the last four digits of the card; the PAN and cvv are never stored, returned, or logged, and every DTO masks its card data in toString. That last point is practical - it makes card data safe even from sloppy debug logs. On observability: the app exposes health and Prometheus metrics, and because the audit node guards on terminal states, the metrics cannot be polluted by unknown outcomes. I should be transparent: card data is not tokenized in this exercise - in production, tokenization is the first thing I would add.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
</slide>
